# Plane Web Frontend — Current Branding Inventory

> A complete, categorized inventory of everything tied to the current **"Plane"** brand in the web
> frontend, so it can be systematically rebranded.
>
> - **Current brand:** Plane — by *Plane Software, Inc.*, GitHub org `makeplane`, domain `plane.so`.
> - **Generated:** 2026-07-02 (branch `preview`). File:line refs are relative to repo root.

---

## 0. Scope, method & how to use this doc

Audited the **web frontend** (`apps/web`) **plus the shared workspace packages it consumes** where
branding actually lives:

| Path | Role | Branding? |
|------|------|-----------|
| `apps/web` | Main web app (Vite + React Router SPA) | ✅ assets, `<head>` meta, hardcoded strings, links |
| `packages/constants` | Shared constants (URLs, metadata, plans) | ✅ **central** brand URLs / metadata / plan names |
| `packages/i18n` | Localization — 19 locales | ✅ **most** user-facing copy |
| `packages/propel` | Design-system / icon library | ✅ **the logo & wordmark SVG components** |
| `packages/ui`, `packages/editor` | Shared UI / rich-text editor | ⚠️ only license-header comments — no user-facing brand text |

**Out of scope** (separate frontends that reuse the packages above): `apps/space`, `apps/admin`,
`apps/live`, `apps/api`. Editing the shared packages covers a lot of them automatically, but their
own `public/` assets and `<head>` meta must be audited separately if the rebrand is product-wide.

**Method:** `ripgrep`/`find` sweeps + parallel exploration agents over the scope, then direct
verification of asset references and the central constants files.

**How to read the entries:** each item shows `path:line` → the exact current value → a short note.
Categories map 1:1 to the request:
1. Non-functional texts · 2. Favicons & brand icons · 3. External links · 4. Images/logos/media · 5. Functional texts.

